      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 407: 🟡 This still updates stored trust requests by local receive time only. With the new sender timestamp, an older/passively redelivered request can arrive later, pass `received \u003e req-\u003esecond.received`, and overwrite `req-\u003esecond.invited` with an older invite time; that regressed value is then saved and synced to other devices. Compare the effective invite ordering timestamp (`invited` when set, otherwise `received`) against the existing request\u0027s effective timestamp before replacing the stored request.",
